# Crossfire Basin - the default skirmish scenario.
#
# Human-readable map format, parsed by apps/client/src/map.rs (one entity per
# line; see docs/maps.md for the full spec):
#
#   name <map name>
#   hq|barracks|turret     <player> <x> <z>
#   infantry|worker|heavy  <player> <x> <z>
#   ore|carbon             <x> <z>
#
# Coordinates are integer world units on the battlefield (-512..512 on both
# axes). '#' starts a comment, blank lines are ignored, and resource nodes
# are always neutral. Player 0 is the human; players 1-3 are bot commanders.
# A standard map carries FOUR spawns (one per corner); the match spawns only
# the entities whose owner is actually playing (1 human + the lobby's bot
# count), so a 1v1 uses the SW/NE diagonal and 3-4 players fill the corners.
#
# Layout, with StarCraft map design as the guide:
#
#   - Classic start: every player opens with an HQ (Astromancer Spire /
#     Hollowmen Command HQ) and four workers on the ore line - production
#     buildings are constructed in-game by workers, never given for free.
#   - Every main base has a 6-patch ore line arced BEHIND the base (between
#     the base and the map edge) so the worker line is defensible ground,
#     with a carbon geyser capping one flank of the line.
#   - Each main has a natural expansion cluster one lane out toward the
#     middle: closer to the fight, cheap to take, harder to hold.
#   - The center is a rich contested cluster (6 ore + 2 carbon) exposed
#     from every lane: the "gold expansion" worth fighting over.
#   - Two side clusters hug the east/west edges at mid-map: third bases
#     that reward controlling the flanking routes.
#   - Shared clusters are mirrored left/right and top/bottom, so no
#     spawn has a shorter path to any contested patch.
#
#               NW main (P2)        NE main (P1)
#                  (ore+gas)           (ore+gas)
#                    NW natural   NE natural
#       west side                          east side
#       cluster          center            cluster
#                       (rich)
#                    SW natural   SE natural
#               SW main (P0)        SE main (P3)
#                  (ore+gas)           (ore+gas)

name Crossfire Basin

# ----------------------------------------------------------- player main (SW)
# StarCraft-style start: the HQ and four workers staged on the ore line,
# which arcs behind the base toward the south edge; geyser on the west flank.
hq 0 -150 190

worker 0 -159 201
worker 0 -153 202
worker 0 -147 202
worker 0 -141 201

ore -173 209
ore -165 216
ore -155 220
ore -145 220
ore -135 216
ore -127 209
carbon -188 198

